WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.036
 James, Paul-- congratulations.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.537
You've made it to the third
round of this competition,

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.205
which means you're
both one step closer

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.207
to the title of "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.376
and a check for $10,000.

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:13.546
When you came here, you used
our forge to create push knives.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.481
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:18.317
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:23.156
And that weapon
is the Katzbalger.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.026
Introduced during
the Renaissance

00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:29.395
in the late 15th
century, the Katzbalger

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.964
became the main sidearm
for European soldiers

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:33.533
known as Landsknechts.

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:36.068
A dominant military
force, these soldiers

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.338
defended the Holy Roman
Empire in times of unrest.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.441
Designed for close
hand-to-hand combat,

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:44.376
the Katzbalger was often
shorter than other broad swords,

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:47.380
but quick and
efficient in action.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.816
Soldiers wielded these
weapons in deadly ambushes,

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:55.321
using devious tactics to lure
the enemy into fatal attacks.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.489
Its sturdy build and
broad, sharp blade

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.092
made it a powerful chopper,
while its signature

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:03.762
S-shaped guard was
instrumental in defense.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:05.097
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:07.333
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:07.866
 Good luck, man.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.701
 Good luck, man.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.841
 It's day one in the
challenge and we're in Moose

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:17.376
Pass at the family forge.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.946
I'm excited to get to work.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.916
OK, the fire is lit.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.383
Hopefully we get the
blade forged out today,

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:27.053
the tang and the fullers--
hey, that's our blade--

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.654
and get a good start on the day.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.890
OK, here we go.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.225
We're going to start
making a blade.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:39.999
A piece of steel is
too wide this way.

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:41.701
It's three and a
half inches this way,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:42.802
and it can't be over two.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.470
So I gotta bring it this way.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.707
If I press-- move too much metal
at once, this will fold over.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.041
It's called a taco.

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:51.076
And there'll be a bad
spot in your steel.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.778
Small bites, no tacos--

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.914
we don't like tacos.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.281
I'm probably a little
behind schedule

00:01:56.381 --> 00:01:57.717
right now, where I wanted to be.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:00.386
I was hoping to get a little
farther with the blade.

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:01.921
And this really
bites me in the butt.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:05.691
Imagine, it's going to turn
into something straight--

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.493
maybe.

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.398
JAMES: It feels good to be home.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:15.067
Best-case scenario for day
one, get the blade forged up.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.202
Worst-case scenario
is the shop explodes

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:19.205
and we all die horribly.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.840
My biggest concern
is the fuller.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:22.341
I've never put one in a blade.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.944 line:0%
First thing I'm trying
is the guillotine fuller.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.480 line:0%
It could work well, but
it's muscle powered.

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.218
That didn't work.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:35.221
Guillotine is not working
nearly as much as it needs to.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:38.024
I have to stop and figure
something else try.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:40.960
Plan B, I need to use
a set of spring fullers

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.361
under my power hammer.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.831
Her name is Gunhilda,
which means battle maiden.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.269
That's good.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:50.302
I've got my fuller.

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:51.871
It actually looks pretty decent.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:54.073
Feeling pretty sweaty right now.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.975
PAUL: Today is day
three of the challenge.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.309
I'm a little behind
where I wanted to be.

00:02:57.409 --> 00:03:00.813 line:7%
But hopefully we can catch up.

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:01.580 line:7%
No.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.982
[bleep] damn.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.383
Whoo.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.054
You start moving too fast,
you just build problems.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:12.191
Today I'm going to put
our hand guard on there.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.894
Aw, I don't know this
is a saveable billet.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.730
Oh no.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.332
I'm having a few obstacles.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.533
[bleep]

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.470
A handguard got overpressed
and it got too thin.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.971
[bleep] damn it.

00:03:26.071 --> 00:03:28.274
So that means I start over.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.843
It's tough when
you have a failure

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:33.012
like I had on the handguard.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:33.979
It cost me four hours.

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.148
It set us behind a bunch.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.484 line:7%
[bleep] done.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.853 line:7%
 Agh.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.021
Ready to go.

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.255
To be successful
today, I definitely

00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:45.123
need to be through
with the heat treatment

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.193
and on to the rest
of the process.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:49.128
The deadline looms ever closer.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.863
But I'm not worried
about it, unless I

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:53.132
have something major screw up.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:56.802
Ugh, there's a big
old nasty warp in it.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.071
[bleep]

00:03:59.137 --> 00:04:01.407
PAUL: It's morning of day five.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.675
And today, we've got
a lot of work to do.

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:05.878
We're going to finish
off our handguard,

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.046
and then a lot of grinding.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.348
I'll put this down
here like this.

00:04:09.414 --> 00:04:12.017
Then I'll wrap this around here.

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:13.252
There we go.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.821
It's going to look
something like that.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:18.357
You know, I'm really feeling
the time crunch right now.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.827
And I still have
to sharpen my edge.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.028
See if I can get an edge on it.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.804
Day five was rough.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.872
I'm done.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:35.975
JAMES: I'm feeling fairly
comfortable about the condition

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.343
of the blade.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:40.113
I did a second heat treat
to get the warp out.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.181
Now I'm going to get
the handle assembled.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:44.183
I've got to get the grip shaped.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:45.418
I don't have time to waste.

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:53.726
That actually feels
pretty decent.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.561
I don't want to send this
sword to the competition

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:57.764
without thoroughly testing it.

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:58.931
Just a little off the top.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.339
Tastes like victory.

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:09.742
 Gentlemen, this is
the strength test--

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.277
a smith's nightmare.

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:12.745
So what we'll do is
we'll take your blades.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:15.314
We'll lock them into
our vise over here

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.116
and fire one round
from this pistol.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:21.620
Now, if your blade's strong, it
should just split that bullet.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:24.256
If not, we could
have a blade shatter.

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:25.258
James, you're up first.

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:26.024
You ready?

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:26.859
 Ready.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:30.963
 OK-- 3, 2, 1, fire.

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:33.933
[gun firing]

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:38.871
JAMES: The blade
is still intact.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:39.872
I can't see any damage.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.374
So we're good to this point.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:44.443
 You can actually see
where it left a little bit

00:05:44.509 --> 00:05:46.345
of that bullet on your blade.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:49.849
There's the tiniest deformation.

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:52.318
Other than that,
everything's still together.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:53.118
Good job.

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:54.186
Nicely done.

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:54.987
All right, Paul.
It's your turn.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:55.754
You ready?

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:56.422
 I'm ready.

00:05:56.489 --> 00:06:00.892
 OK-- 3, 2, 1, fire.

00:06:00.959 --> 00:06:04.497
[gun firing]

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.236
 I see the bullet splits,
blade doesn't fly in half,

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:12.772
which was a relief.

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:15.508
That's almost
identical damage, Paul.

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:18.310
Again, you can see where the
bullet left a little scar

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:20.246
around along the side.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.179
All right, good job.

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:22.481
 Thank you.

00:06:22.581 --> 00:06:24.583
 Bladesmiths, to see how
sharp your weapons are,

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:26.953
I will take your sword
and deliver a slash

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:29.154
using each side of your blade.

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:30.956
And I'll deliver a thrust.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:31.924
James, you're up first.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:32.692
You ready?

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:33.659
 Let's do it.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.006
All right, James, let's
talk about your sword.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:49.075
Your edge is razor sharp.

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:53.513
On the delivery downward,
it was easily into the bag

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.314
and slashed into it.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:58.084
Your tip, not coming
to an exact point,

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:59.351
but because of
that edge geometry,

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:01.987
was easy enough to
thrust into this bag.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:04.090
And your blade will cut.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:04.856
Good job.

00:07:04.923 --> 00:07:06.191
 Thanks.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:07.326
 Paul, you're up next.
You ready?

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:08.561
- I'm ready.
- Let's do this.

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:25.311
All right, Paul, on
the cuts over here,

00:07:25.377 --> 00:07:27.179
it starts to lacerate,
but not deeply

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:28.647
enough to go into the bag.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:31.783
The edge geometry you
have of your tip over here

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:34.320
isn't as sharp as I
thought it would be.

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.222
This did not penetrate
the bag at all.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:40.426
When you flipped it over, same
thing also with the other edge.

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:44.163
It did lacerate,
but not as deep.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:47.866
Overall, your blade
will still cut--

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:48.701
not as deeply.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.102
 Good deal.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:51.571
 Next up is the kill test.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:56.108
The Katzbalger is a weapon that
was used in history to kill.

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:58.544
I will take your sword and
I'll deliver lethal blows

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.412
on this big carcass.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:01.880
James, you're up first.
You ready?

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:02.448
 Let's do it.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.149
 Let's do this.

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:15.962
All right, James, let's
talk about your blade.

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:20.999
This section right here, it
nicely sliced into the carcass.

00:08:21.066 --> 00:08:24.436
It chopped through the
spine into some bone.

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:28.006
And overall, your
blade will kill.

00:08:28.106 --> 00:08:29.007
 Thank you.

00:08:29.074 --> 00:08:29.575
 Good job.

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:30.542
Paul, you ready?

00:08:30.609 --> 00:08:31.244
 I'm ready.

00:08:42.888 --> 00:08:43.523
Nope.

00:08:46.224 --> 00:08:50.061
 Well, Paul, unfortunately,
your edge over here, some areas

00:08:50.128 --> 00:08:52.064
are rolled.

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:53.499
And it hit the mark.

00:08:53.565 --> 00:08:56.468
But it did not lacerate
or cut into the pig.

00:08:56.568 --> 00:08:59.471
So, unfortunately, your
blade will not kill.

00:08:59.572 --> 00:09:01.840
 No edge at all.

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:03.442
 Gentlemen, I
know you've worked

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:04.944
very hard on your blades.

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:07.312
But in this arena, there can
only be one "Forged in Fire"

00:09:07.379 --> 00:09:08.313
champion.

00:09:08.413 --> 00:09:11.517
And that champion is James.

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:12.718
Congratulations.

00:09:12.785 --> 00:09:13.952
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:15.221
 Thank you.

00:09:15.321 --> 00:09:17.823
 Paul, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:09:17.889 --> 00:09:21.260
Paul, please,
surrender your weapon.

00:09:21.327 --> 00:09:23.461
PAUL: I absolutely agree
with the judges' decision.

00:09:23.562 --> 00:09:24.630
- Paul, thanks so much.
- Thanks.

00:09:24.697 --> 00:09:25.664
Appreciate you guys.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:26.531
I mean, I just ran out of time.

00:09:26.598 --> 00:09:28.266
There was nothing else.

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:29.067
 Congratulations, man.

00:09:29.167 --> 00:09:30.436
 Thank you.

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:31.670
His blade performed the
way it was supposed to.

00:09:31.736 --> 00:09:34.906
And mine performed like a spoon.

00:09:34.973 --> 00:09:36.942
I may not be the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:37.008 --> 00:09:39.978
but ladies, I'm single
and ready to mingle.

00:09:40.078 --> 00:09:41.246
Call me.

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:42.781
Love to dance.

00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.016
 James, congratulations.

00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:45.618
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:09:45.685 --> 00:09:48.154
and will be leaving here
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:48.854
Good job.

00:09:48.921 --> 00:09:51.257
 Thank you.

00:09:51.324 --> 00:09:53.459
I'm the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:53.525 --> 00:09:55.428
I will never win
points for prettiness,

00:09:55.494 --> 00:09:58.030
but the tests here or
on the battlefield,

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.865
it's not the pretty
weapon that wins.

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:00.999
 Good job.

00:10:01.066 --> 00:10:02.634
 I'm very lucky to be
able to make a living

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:03.969
creating something useful.

00:10:04.069 --> 00:10:06.872
And I will use my winnings
to make more blades.

00:10:06.973 --> 00:10:10.376
[theme music]

